systemcraft/books/
*.epub

# Content Machine private brain (2026-08-24, build map GitHub #158) — the
# machine itself (.claude/skills/content-machine/, README, contracts) is
# tracked publicly; its private brain is local-only. The corpus is verbatim
# Sean — raw interview answers, hand-edits, pre-AI prose — and is the
# irreplaceable input the whole machine reads from. The ledger holds the
# consent-gated lessons loop, the cheese bank the labeled negative specimens,
# do-not-promote.md the subjects Sean has ruled off-limits, and
# reference-universe.md the personal-history and pop-culture library the
# voice pass draws anchors from (merged from two elicitations per #174).
# Given its own home (NOT under .claude/skills/writing-voice-modes/references/,
# which L2/L10 schedule for demolition) per wayfinder ticket #160.
# Never `git add` these; never paste their contents into a tracked file or a
# GitHub issue.
creative-studio/content-machine/corpus/
creative-studio/content-machine/ledger/
creative-studio/content-machine/cheese-bank/
creative-studio/content-machine/reference-universe.md
creative-studio/content-machine/do-not-promote.md
creative-studio/content-machine/transcripts/
# X stimulus blocks (2026-09-05, wayfinder #250). X's stage 2 is not an
# interview: the reactive route's artifact is someone else's post, fetched
# verbatim through publish.x.com/oembed. It is ignored for two reasons. It is
# an unpublished editorial artifact in a public repo — the file names the slug
# of a piece that has not shipped and records what he is considering answering.
# And it sits in a directory the gates must be able to distinguish from
# transcripts on sight: a block has the OPPOSITE polarity (forbidden strings,
# never permitted vocabulary), so it gets its own home beside them rather than
# a filename convention inside theirs.
creative-studio/content-machine/stimulus/
# Handoff drafts and Sean's finals, per piece (2026-09-04, wayfinder #232 — the
# first X run). A draft is derived entirely from git-ignored inputs (the
# transcript, the corpus, voice-samples.md) and is unpublished until Sean ships
# it, so it inherits their privacy class. The lessons loop needs the handoff and
# the final side by side on disk to diff, so they get a durable private home
# rather than a scratch directory.
creative-studio/content-machine/pieces/
# Spread-run (#221) assembled shaping contexts. `context-full.md` and
# `context-stripped.md` are verbatim concatenations of the transcript, all six
# corpus files, voice-samples.md and reference-universe.md — every one of them
# ignored above — written into a TRACKED public path so single-shot API arms
# could be given byte-identical input. `voice-samples-stripped.md` is likewise a
# verbatim copy minus the quarantined sections (#224). The drafts, scripts,
# measurements and session record in that folder stay tracked; these three
# never do. Caught 2026-09-01 before the first commit.
vault/20_projects/substack-studio/spread-run/context-full.md
vault/20_projects/substack-studio/spread-run/context-stripped.md
vault/20_projects/substack-studio/spread-run/voice-samples-stripped.md
# Agentic-CLI reasoning traces. Codex's stderr quotes the private files it was
# told to read — 240KB carrying the transcript, corpus excerpts and Sean's
# verbatim answers. Any CLI that reads the private brain writes its own copy of
# it into whatever log you capture. The OpenRouter/local logs here are clean
# (JSON usage summaries only) and stay tracked.
vault/20_projects/substack-studio/spread-run/codex.log
# Coined-lines ledger (#162): the one-artifact rule needs a record of his best
# lines and which piece spent each one. Public repo, so the record stays local.
creative-studio/content-machine/coined-lines.md
# Oracle ideas bank (#169): banked spike cards quote Sean's commits, dailies,
# partner-session sidecars and fleet manifests. It lives here rather than in a
# vault note because vault/20_projects/substack-studio/ is a tracked public
# path, and an ideas note there would publish the sweep a card at a time.
creative-studio/content-machine/ideas-bank.md
# Oracle listening reports (#239): the week's AI-news brief the Oracle renders
# to local TTS, plus the raw news pull and the gists feed beside it. The report
# names his spikes and the experiment cards each news item spawned, so it is
# private for the same reason the ideas bank is. The MP3 goes to
# vault/90_system/audio/, ignored above. Canary-tested before the first report
# existed: `git add` refuses the directory.
creative-studio/content-machine/oracle-reports/

